+# Pitch 03 — what a hardwood quote is actually made of
+
+**Targets:** personal-finance and home-economics desks, real-estate
+aggregators, renovation-cost verticals, design blogs that run buyer guides.
+
+**Why this angle lands:** everyone publishes a price range and nobody publishes
+the mechanism. We publish both, with the commodity inputs live from the Bank of
+Canada — which is a data story, and data stories get linked.
+
+**What we can put behind it:**
+
+- `/market` — forestry, energy and USD/CAD, pulled live from the Bank of Canada,
+  with the mechanism behind each and why it is volatile
+- `/api/market` — the same data as JSON, CORS-open, no key
+- `/guides/how-to-evaluate-a-hardwood-quote` — the published criteria
+- `/framework/assess` — score any quote, from anyone
+- Price bands: `/services`, published as full bands rather than starting-from
+  numbers
+
+**Note before sending:** the ROI framing in the original brief — premium oak
+versus builder-grade, as a resale return — needs a source we do not have. Do not
+assert a resale figure. The version below makes the cost-mechanism argument
+instead, which is the part we can actually evidence.
+
+---
+
+**Subject:** We publish the commodity inputs behind a hardwood quote, live. Use
+them.
+
+Hi [Name],
+
+Every renovation guide prints a price range for hardwood flooring. None of them
+explain why the range moves, which is the part a reader can actually act on.
+
+So we published the inputs. Three series, pulled live from the Bank of Canada,
+each with the mechanism written out and why it is volatile:
+
+https://ecowoods.ca/market
+
+- **Forestry commodity prices** — the raw material
+- **Energy** — kiln drying and freight, both energy-intensive, both
+  passed through
+- **USD/CAD** — most engineered product and nearly all finish chemistry is
+  priced in US dollars
+
+The same data as JSON, no key, CORS-open, free to chart:
+https://ecowoods.ca/api/market
+
+We also publish our own price bands as full bands rather than starting-from
+numbers — https://ecowoods.ca/services — and a scoring framework a reader can
+run against any contractor's quote, ours included:
+https://ecowoods.ca/framework/assess
+
+If a cost piece is on your calendar, take the data. Attribution appreciated, not
+required — it is CC BY. And if you want the mechanism explained on the record for
+a quote, I am happy to do that in fifteen minutes.
+
+[Name]
